Here are some examples of beginner yoga poses:

Child’s pose, where you sit on your knees and bend forward, arms by your sides, like a child crawling;
Downward facing dog, where you lift your hips up and spread your knees wide to form a low squat, toes back, arms long, palms facing upward, shoulders relaxed;
The sun salutation, which involves standing, raising your arms, bending forward, returning to stand, bending forward, raising your arms, and then repeating three times;
Bridge pose, where you lie flat on your back, raise your hips, and bring your shoulders, feet, and arms into the air;
Seated cross-legged, where you sit on the floor, cross your legs in front of you, and raise your arms overhead;
Tree pose, where you stand, bring your feet together, raise your arms overhead, and bend forward;
Squat pose, where you crouch down, feet together, knees apart, and extend your arms forward.
